Here are the **best 20 CloudWatch Logs Insights queries for Amazon Connect contact flow logs**.

## 1. One contact’s full journey

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Parameters, Results, @message
| filter ContactId = "CONTACT_ID_HERE" or @message like /CONTACT_ID_HERE/
| sort @timestamp asc
| limit 500
```

## 2. Latest contact flow errors

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /ERROR|Error|Exception|Failed|Failure|Timeout|Timed out/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 3. Error count over time

```sql
fields @timestamp, @message
| filter @message like /ERROR|Error|Exception|Failed|Failure|Timeout|Timed out/
| stats count(*) as errorCount by bin(5m)
| sort @timestamp desc
```

## 4. Top failing flow blocks

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /ERROR|Error|Exception|Failed|Failure|Timeout/
| stats count(*) as failures by ContactFlowName, Identifier
| sort failures desc
| limit 30
```

## 5. Lambda invocation failures

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Lambda|Invoke AWS Lambda function|FunctionArn/
| filter @message like /ERROR|Error|Exception|Failed|Timeout|AccessDenied|ResourceNotFound|Unhandled/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 6. Lambda calls by flow/block

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactFlowName, Identifier, @message
| filter @message like /Lambda|Invoke AWS Lambda function|FunctionArn/
| stats count(*) as lambdaCalls by ContactFlowName, Identifier
| sort lambdaCalls desc
| limit 50
```

## 7. Lex bot issues

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Lex|Bot|Intent|Slot|NoInput|NoMatch|Fallback/
| filter @message like /ERROR|Error|Failed|NoInput|NoMatch|Fallback|Timeout/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 8. Lex intent results

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Lex|Intent/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 9. Transfer failures

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Transfer|Queue|Agent/
| filter @message like /Failed|Failure|Error|At capacity|No agents|Timeout/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 10. Queue-related events

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Parameters, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Queue|Transfer to queue|Set working queue|Get queue metrics|Enqueue/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 150
```

## 11. Disconnect or hang-up events

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Disconnect|disconnected|Customer disconnect|Contact disconnected|Hangup|Hang up/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 12. Customer input / DTMF issues

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Parameters, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Get customer input|Store customer input|DTMF|NoInput|NoMatch|Input/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 150
```

## 13. NoInput and NoMatch count

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactFlowName, Identifier, @message
| filter @message like /NoInput|NoMatch/
| stats count(*) as count by ContactFlowName, Identifier
| sort count desc
| limit 30
```

## 14. Prompt or audio playback errors

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Play prompt|Prompt|Audio|S3/
| filter @message like /ERROR|Error|Failed|AccessDenied|NoSuchKey|not found|Invalid/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 15. Contact attribute issues

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Parameters, Results, @message
| filter @message like /Attribute|Contact attribute/
| filter @message like /Invalid|null|empty|not found|missing|Failed|Error/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 16. Permission and access issues

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Results, @message
| filter @message like /AccessDenied|Unauthorized|not authorized|permission|KMS|IAM|Forbidden/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 100
```

## 17. Find calls by phone number

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Parameters, Results, @message
| filter @message like /PHONE_NUMBER_HERE/
| sort @timestamp asc
| limit 300
```

## 18. High-volume contact flows

```sql
fields ContactFlowName
| stats count(*) as eventCount by ContactFlowName
| sort eventCount desc
| limit 20
```

## 19. Most active flow blocks

```sql
fields ContactFlowName, Identifier
| stats count(*) as eventCount by ContactFlowName, Identifier
| sort eventCount desc
| limit 50
```

## 20. Best all-in-one troubleshooting query

```sql
fields @timestamp, ContactId, ContactFlowName, Identifier, Parameters, Results, @message
| filter @message like /ERROR|Error|Exception|Failed|Failure|Timeout|Timed out|AccessDenied|Unauthorized|ResourceNotFound|NoSuchKey|NoInput|NoMatch|Fallback|Disconnect|Transfer/
| sort @timestamp desc
| limit 200
```
Use this for **Lambda duration for one specific Amazon Connect ContactId**.

## 1. Find Lambda logs for one ContactId

```sql
fields @timestamp, @message, @logStream
| filter @message like /CONTACT_ID_HERE/
| sort @timestamp asc
| limit 300
```

## 2. If your Lambda logs include ContactId and REPORT lines

```sql
fields @timestamp, @requestId, @duration, @billedDuration, @maxMemoryUsed, @memorySize, @message
| filter @type = "REPORT"
| filter @message like /CONTACT_ID_HERE/
| sort @timestamp asc
| limit 100
```

But note: **Lambda REPORT lines usually do not contain the ContactId** unless your Lambda logs it on the same request context. Better approach below.

## 3. Best approach: map ContactId to Lambda requestId

First, find the Lambda request ID from application logs:

```sql
fields @timestamp, @requestId, @message
| filter @message like /CONTACT_ID_HERE/
| sort @timestamp asc
| limit 100
```

Copy the `@requestId`, then run:

```sql
fields @timestamp, @requestId, @duration, @billedDuration, @maxMemoryUsed, @memorySize
| filter @type = "REPORT"
| filter @requestId = "LAMBDA_REQUEST_ID_HERE"
| limit 20
```

## 4. If ContactId is stored as JSON field

```sql
fields @timestamp, contactId, @requestId, @message
| filter contactId = "CONTACT_ID_HERE"
| sort @timestamp asc
| limit 100
```

Then use the request ID:

```sql
fields @timestamp, @requestId, @duration, @billedDuration, @maxMemoryUsed, @memorySize
| filter @type = "REPORT"
| filter @requestId = "LAMBDA_REQUEST_ID_HERE"
| limit 20
```

## 5. Best combined query when ContactId appears in Lambda logs

```sql
fields @timestamp, @type, @requestId, @duration, @billedDuration, @maxMemoryUsed, @memorySize, @message
| filter @message like /CONTACT_ID_HERE/ or @requestId = "LAMBDA_REQUEST_ID_HERE"
| sort @timestamp asc
| limit 300
```

Replace:

```text
CONTACT_ID_HERE
LAMBDA_REQUEST_ID_HERE
```

Best practical workflow:

```sql
fields @timestamp, @requestId, @message
| filter @message like /CONTACT_ID_HERE/
| sort @timestamp asc
| limit 100
```

Then:

```sql
fields @timestamp, @requestId, @duration, @billedDuration, @maxMemoryUsed, @memorySize
| filter @type = "REPORT"
| filter @requestId = "PASTE_REQUEST_ID_HERE"
```
